  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nPer the current spec it doesn't seem to do anything special on `none`, as neither of [update](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#update-a-color-well-control-color) or [serialize](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#serialize-a-color-well-control-color) steps are doing anything to a display-p3 color after [parsing](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#parse-color) it. (Parsing includes [resolving](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#resolving-color-values) in this case, but it doesn't seem to do anything with `none` values either.)\n\nCurrently [WPT expects none to be resolved as 0](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/a564417be56ae6880d5b9ab72731f2272e5a7cff/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/color.window.js#L244-L245) and WebKit passes it, perhaps either it should not or the spec should do something extra?\n\ncc @emilio @annevk ",
